rdin had run out of his lane and was disqualified from the AAU, but declared winner of the Olympic Trials and placed on the team."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final in Los Angeles matched these four, who would constitute four consecutive gold medalists in the event – Taylor in 1924, Burghley in 1928, Hardin would win in " [:a {:href "/results/58244"} "1936"] ", and Tisdall won in 1932. He took an early lead, but knocked over the last hurdle, allowing Hardin to close to within two metres. The downed hurdle cost Tisdall the world and Olympic record of 51.7, both reverting to Hardin in second place. In accordance with the rules at the time, Tisdall’s official time was rounded up to 51.8, to the nearest fifth."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "253"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/71597"} "Bob Tisdall"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRL.png"}] "IRL"]] [:td {} "54.8 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "52.8 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "51.8 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "430"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78512"} "Glenn Hardin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "55.0 (3 h2)"] [:td {} "52.8 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "51.9 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "460"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79115"} "Morgan Taylor"]] [:td {} [:a {:href